 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Push notifications
+
+Push notifications are signed with a VAPID key pair. In development and test, Fizzy generates a throwaway pair on boot, so you can turn notifications on for your browser from Notification Settings without any setup.
+
+Generate a pair of your own with `bin/rails push:vapid_keys`, and export them as `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` if you want your subscriptions to survive a restart. That's also how they're configured in production.
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
