@@ -101,6 +101,25 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications
+
+Fizzy can push notifications to the browsers and phones people use, so anything that lands in someone's notification tray reaches their devices too.
+Push services need your instance to identify itself with a VAPID key pair, which you can generate with:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm ghcr.io/basecamp/fizzy:main bin/rails push:vapid_keys
+```
+
+Set the two values it prints:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`
+
+Keep them stable: if the keys change, everyone has to turn notifications back on for their devices.
+Without them, push notifications are simply not offered — email notifications and the notification tray keep working as usual.
+
+Everyone turns push notifications on for themselves, per device, from their Notification Settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
